{"id":"u-5e04aa59-1bff-437f-b26f-5af325f30dc4","src":"community","title":"Dad Strength","author":"Gabriel D.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/W1Tqgo-dad-strength","desc":"Dad Strength is a 6-week program designed to build a strong, athletic, and imposing physique — focusing on hypertrophy, progressive overload, and consistency.\n\nThe proposal is simple: train hard, recover well, and build a body that truly looks strong.\n\nThe program uses 3 Full Body sessions per week, with low volume, high execution quality, and sets performed close to failure. Each workout strategically distributes stimuli to allow for high muscle frequency without accumulating unnecessary fatigue.\n\nProgram priorities\n\nForearms — the key differentiator of the physique, aiming for thickness, density, and grip strength.\n\nChest — a full and projected chest, built through presses and isolation movements.\n\nCalves — high frequency and volume to develop visually complete legs.\n\nTraps and neck — creating a thicker, stronger, and more imposing upper structure.\n\nShoulders — especially lateral delts and vertical presses to build width.\n\nGlutes — strength, volume, and support to complete the athletic structure.\n\nArms, back, quads, hamstrings, and abs continue to be trained to maintain a balanced and functional physique.\n\nProgression system\n\nDad Strength uses double progression.\n\nEach exercise has a rep range. The goal is to gradually increase reps while maintaining proper form, and once you reach the top of the range, increase the load and restart the cycle.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":3,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-29T07:59:44.785Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"r":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"x":2}]},{"n":"Latera